If you've watched the movie "National Treasure," you might think there's a treasure map written behind the Declaration of Independence.
However, that is not true. Just because something is written behind a document does not mean that the document is a treasure map.
Behind the Declaration of Independence, the following text was written: "Original Declaration of Independence, July 4, 1776." The text appears upside down at the bottom of the document.
Although no one yet knows who wrote it, it is well known that this large manuscript codex, measuring 29¾ inches by 24½ inches, was originally hung for preservation in its early days.
Therefore, it is possible that the note is merely attached as a label.
