If you show some basic courtesy, the Parisians' seemingly unexpected behavior will immediately disappear.
Plitvice Lakes National Park is rich in forest cover and predominantly consists of various types of beech, spruce, and fir trees, featuring a mix of Alpine and Mediterranean vegetation.
It has a notably wide variety of flora due to its diverse microclimates, different soils, and varied altitudes.
This region is also the habitat of a wide variety of animal and bird species.
Rare animals such as the European brown bear, wolf, eagle, owl, blackbird, wild cat, and forest raven can be found here alongside many other common species.
