The pronunciation of Italian words is relatively simple, as the pronunciation of most words exactly matches their spelling.
The letters you need to be careful with are C and G, as their pronunciation varies depending on the vowels that follow them.
Also, be careful to pronounce r and rr differently: "caro" means dear, whereas "carro" means cart.
