Since light pollution was not initially considered a problem, but is now regarded as one, they are usually located in cities or on university campuses, and are easier to access than those built during the modern era.
Most modern research telescopes are large facilities located in remote areas with favorable atmospheric conditions.
Viewing cherry blossoms (hanami) has been part of Japanese culture since the 8th century.
This concept originates from China, where the selected flower was the plum blossom.
In Japan, the first cherry blossom ceremony is held exclusively for the Emperor and the close members of the imperial court.
