Christmas is one of the most important holidays in Christianity and is celebrated as the birthday of Jesus Christ.
Many of these holiday traditions have also been adopted by people in Christian countries who do not adhere to this religion, as well as non-Christians around the world.
There is a tradition of staying awake on the night of Eid al-Fitr in places that are visible, so that one can witness the sunrise.
Of course, Christianity has religious justifications for this tradition, but it can well be said that it may have originally been a celebration of spring and fertility predating Christianity.
Most traditional churches usually hold the Easter Vigil on Saturday night during the Easter holiday, while this congregation often gathers at midnight to celebrate Christ's resurrection.
All animals that initially arrived at the islands came here either by swimming, flying, or floating.
Due to the great distance from the continent, mammals were unable to reach there, so the giant tortoise is the largest animal that grazes in the Galápagos.
Since humans arrived in the Galápagos, many mammals—including goats, horses, cattle, mice, cats, and dogs—have been introduced to these islands.
If you visit the North or South Pole during winter, you'll witness the polar night, meaning the sun does not rise above the horizon.
This provides a good opportunity to see the aurora, as the sky will be fairly dark throughout the day.
Since these areas are sparsely populated and, precisely because of this, light pollution is not usually a problem, you can also enjoy the stars.
Japanese work culture is more hierarchical and formal than what Westerners are accustomed to.
The clothes are standard work attire, and colleagues address each other by their surnames or job titles.
Harmony in the workplace is very important, and instead of praising individual achievements, emphasis should be placed on group efforts.
Workers are often required to obtain approval from their superiors for every decision they make, and they are expected to obey their superiors' instructions without question.
